# Thread 2 — IMPORTANT: `git rm --cached` flips `hasGitChanges` in `developBugAndCreatePR.js`

**Fixed** with the first suggested option (extend the porcelain filter), backed by the requested regression test.

- `js/common/gitStaging.js` (new shared module, see Thread 3) now exposes `isRuntimeArtifactStatusLine(line)`; the filter in `js/developBugAndCreatePR.js` skips those lines exactly the way it already skipped `factory-kit`:

```js
const statusLines = rawStatus.split('\n').filter(function(l) {
    return l.trim() &&
           !/^(\?\?|A )\s+factory-kit(\/|$)/.test(l) &&
           // gh-628: `--cached` untracking leaves the runtime logs
           // on disk as untracked files — never the agent's work,
           // so they must not flip hasGitChanges (round 1 review).
           !gitStaging.isRuntimeArtifactStatusLine(l) &&
           ...
});
```

  The shared helper matches any status line naming one of the 7 runtime artifacts (copilot-sessions, credential-helper.log, fa-trace.log, run-output.txt, stall-capture.log, fa-sessions, .dmtools-session-output.log) — so untracked leftovers, staged untrack deletions, and renames are all covered without hand-maintaining a second regex.
- Regression test added in `js/unit-tests/test_developBugAndCreatePR.js`: **"untracked machine-local runtime artifacts alone do not count as git changes (gh-628)"** — a status reporting only `?? .dmtools/...` lines must produce **no** `git checkout -B`/`git commit`/`git push`, and the Jira comment must honestly say *"No partial work was produced."* (fails against the pre-fix code, passes now).
- The interrupted-agent path still fires for real work (`A  outputs/rca.md` etc.) — pinned by the existing partial-work tests, which still pass.
- Full suite: **1331 passed / 0 failed**.

